      "widgets_values": [
        "## ltx-i2v (lab)\n\nWhat this graph does: Image\u2192video (~97f). Set LoadImage to your still.\nModels: LTX distilled FP8 UNET + DualCLIP (gemma_3_12B_it_fp4_mixed + ltx-2.3_text_projection_bf16, type ltxv) + LTX23 video/audio VAEs (joint AV empty audio latents required before KSampler).\nSampler: euler \u00b7 simple \u00b7 CFG 1.0 \u00b7 97 frames @ 24 fps \u2248 4.0 s \u00b7 768\u00d7512.\n\nPRIMARY OUTPUT \u2014 MP4 (easy to watch)\n\u2022 Node: Save video (MP4) = VHS_VideoCombine (format video/h264-mp4, 24 fps).\n\u2022 After Queue: open that node for an inline video preview.\n\u2022 File also under ComfyUI/output/ as ez_ltx_i2v_video_*.mp4 (comfy-state volume).\n\u2022 Frames still saved via SaveImage prefix ez_ltx_i2v_frames for inspection.\n\nPrompting (LTX-2.3 + Gemma DualCLIP):\n\u2022 Describe actions over time (camera path + subject/environment motion).\n\u2022 I2V: restate the still, then one clear camera move + micro-motion; keep identity stable.\n\u2022 Negatives target temporal artifacts (morphing, flicker, jitter) if you raise CFG.\n\nHow to run:\n1. Set LoadImage to your start frame (e.g. Flux still).\n2. Review Motion / prompt; Queue.\n3. Watch Save video (MP4) preview; optional: open output/*.mp4.\n\nStack installs ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite (VHS) + system/imageio ffmpeg.\nJoint AV: LTXVEmptyLatentAudio + concat required; audio latent unused (not saved).\nOptional offline: stitch PNG frames with host ffmpeg if you only need frames."
      ],
      "title": "Operator note \u2014 video output"
    },
